a/float64 x)) :number :bigint)\n   133\t                 (if (js/str? x)\n   134\t                   :string\n   135\t                   (if (js/cell? x)\n   136\t                     (if (= (get (cell/get x) :js/type) :function)\n   137\t                       :function\n   138\t                       (if (= (get (cell/get x) :js/type) :symbol)\n   139\t                         :symbol\n   140\t                         :object))\n   141\t                     ;; An admitted foreign callable that is not a JS\n   142\t                     ;; cell (a clojure descriptor, a bound method) is\n   143\t                     ;; still a function; only a value no profile admits\n   144\t                     ;; keeps the bare-number fallback.\n   145\t                     (if (yang.call/eligible? x) :function :number)))))))))]\n   146\t    [js/ty (fn [k] (if (= k :function) :object k))]\n   147\t    [js/prim-type?\n   148\t     (fn [t]\n   149\t       (if (= t :string)\n   150\t         true\n   151\t         (if (= t :number) true (if (= t :symbol) true (= t :bigint)))))]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"**Verdict: do not land yet.** The new matrix legs exercise the shared composition path, but the implementation has three correctness defects outside those examples.\n\n1. **Projected Clojure globals are erased before the caller runs.** [prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:87) clears `clj.rt/globals` on every `clj/run-main`. The profile projects a foreign export into that table before calling the entry, but also writes it to the task store; ordinary free reads happen to use that second binding. [conformance.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/test/yang/call/conformance.clj:163) Thus the passing leg does not demonstrate projection through the runtime globals. If the caller also defines that name, [lower-unit](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2778) rewrites its reads to `clj/global-get`, where the projected value has already been cleared. Re-entering `clj/run-main` also clears globals captured by an earlier Clojure unit in the same task.\n\n2. **A source map can trigger an invalid cell dereference.** [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1308) routes any map with `:type :cell-ref` to admission, and [admission](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2104) immediately calls `cell/get`. A normal source map such as `{:type :cell-ref}` therefore no longer behaves as an invocable Clojure map; it raises a dead-or-forged-reference VM failure. The VM checks the seal, so this does **not** establish a witness bypass, but the structural test must distinguish source data from an authentic reference or handle refusal without breaking map invocation.\n\n3. **TypeScript still classifies cell-backed foreign functions as objects.** [prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:135) checks `yang.call/eligible?` only after the cell branch. A Python function, for example, is a cell with `:py/type :function` and a call entry, so `js/kind-of` returns `:object` even though the same value is callable. This makes `typeof` and behavior dependent on that classification inconsistent. The TypeScript change is within the round’s scope, but it needs to cover admitted foreign cells as well as non-cell descriptors.\n\nThe donor path does avoid call-node surgery, foreign `:code` extraction, and pair-specific wrappers. The runtime cell itself is task-local and I found no host-side mutation path; the problem is its reset and the profile’s separate store binding. The profile has all the requested keys, but its projection behavior is therefore incomplete.\n\nI could not independently reproduce the reported green suites in this read-only session: `bb test:sub:clj yang.base` stopped at the ANTLR prerequisite lock, with sandbox permission errors. The supplied seat results remain useful evidence for the tested matrix cases, but they do not cover the defects above."}}
